      },
      "message": "fix(post): a touch probe section starts no coolant on any mill post\n\nA section that states a speed of 0 (a touch probe, #523) now resolves\nno coolant in every shipped mill post's preamble - fanuc, haas,\nsinumerik, heidenhain, mazak, doosan-dnm and carvera gate coolantFor()\non the same rpm-0 test tormach already used. Doosan DNM posted M8 for\na probe even with no machine; the others posted the machine's Flood\ncode on any machine that lists one. No coolant on means no M9 for it.\nAn explicit Mist / Air / Through-tool ask on a probe op is neither\nposted nor refused (the probe stays dry).\n\nPinned by crates/app/tests/probe_no_coolant.rs (every mill post, with\nand without a machine stating coolants, explicit asks, the Doosan\nbore-centre probe stream, and a cutting-section control).\n\nFixes #995\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
